body:
@jrouwe I was taking a final quick look at this code, and realized that this could probably be simplified.

Since we clear `area_soft_body_overlaps` before every physics step, we'll presumably never end up in a situation where one of these shape pairs is present in it already, so the `.has(..)` and `.erase(...)` on it are both redundant.

Similarly, we're populating `area_exits` with all the previous `area_soft_body_overlaps` in `_clear_area_soft_body_overlaps()`, since we're relying on the recently added reference counting in `JoltArea3D`, but there's no reason why we couldn't just erase from `area_exits` if we do find a viable overlap, and save us from that extra work, while also avoiding to add to `area_enters` in such a case.

I'm thinking it could look like this instead:

```suggestion
	if (p_area.can_monitor(p_body)) {
		area_soft_body_overlaps.insert(p_shape_pair);
		if (!area_exits.erase(p_shape_pair)) {
			area_enters.insert(p_shape_pair);
		}
	}
}
```

Does that seem right?

